Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-82: a Font.Name drop-down; README: the WPF
 operations, one by one (0.82.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"做到所有WPF 基礎操作都差不多 才叫我檢查" (EastSun 20260930):
- Font.Name has a list (WPF's FontFamily is a drop-down): the .dfm's font, the
  ones this control's font list names, the usual ones (MS Sans Serif,
  Microsoft JhengHei, 新細明體, 標楷體, Arial, Tahoma, ...), no repeats; a name
  picked is set at once; typing still works.
- README 「跟 WPF 設計工具的操作對照」: every basic operation of Microsoft's
  XAML Designer / Events tab / Windows Forms pages next to what this tool does;
  the one it cannot (drag from the toolbox onto the design surface: VS Code
  does not let a side-bar item be dragged into the designer) and the ones that
  do not apply (Grid rails, margins, data binding, resources).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 167, panels, real VS Code 148): panels
(the Font.Name list: 12 names, MS Sans Serif and Arial among them).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
